{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"UmaChallenger","kind":"identifier"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Hand one to ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AxiamGuards\/requireAccess(_:resource:scope:umaChallenge:)","isActive":true},{"text":" and a denial stops","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"being a bare 403: the guard mints a fresh permission ticket for the pair the caller lacked and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"attaches it to the thrown ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AuthzError","isActive":true},{"text":", so the framework adapter can return it as a header and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a UMA-aware client knows where to go for authority instead of only being told “no”.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Opt-in, and deliberately so."}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" Emitting a challenge means minting a credential — a wire call","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to the Protection API, and a live ticket, produced on a path the caller did not explicitly","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"request. A guard that did that on every denial by default would turn each unauthorized request","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"into a Protection API call, which is a denial-of-service amplifier pointed at your own","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"authorization server. So it happens only where an application asked for it.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Failure is not escalation."}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" If minting fails — the PAT expired, the Protection API is down,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the resource declares none of the requested scopes — the denial still surfaces as an ordinary"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AuthzError","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" without a challenge. A caller who was going to be refused is refused either way;"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"letting a Protection API outage turn a deny into a 503 would hand the outage a second"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"consequence, and letting it turn into an allow would be a security bug."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/umachallenger"]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/UmaChallenger"},"metadata":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"UmaChallenger","kind":"identifier"}],"modules":[{"name":"AxiamSDK"}],"roleHeading":"Structure","role":"symbol","symbolKind":"struct","title":"UmaChallenger","externalID":"s:8AxiamSDK13UmaChallengerV","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"UmaChallenger","kind":"identifier"}]},"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK"]]},"relationshipsSections":[{"type":"conformsTo","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/s8SendableP"],"kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A configured "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"WWW-Authenticate: UMA"},{"type":"text","text":" challenge emitter (CONTRACT.md §20.3, emit half)."}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/UmaChallenger\/init(realm:asURI:pat:)"],"title":"Initializers"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/UmaChallenger\/asURI","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/UmaChallenger\/pat","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/UmaChallenger\/realm"],"title":"Instance Properties"}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"references":{"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/AxiamGuards/requireAccess(_:resource:scope:umaChallenge:)":{"title":"requireAccess(_:resource:scope:umaChallenge:)","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/axiamguards\/requireaccess(_:resource:scope:umachallenge:)","type":"topic","abstract":[{"code":"require_access(action, resource[, scope])","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (§11): the ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"authenticated caller","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" must pass","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"an AXIAM authorization check. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"subject_id"},{"text":" is the end user’s id (§11.2 rule 2), not the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"application’s service-account session.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"requireAccess","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"resource","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"scope","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"text":"?, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"umaChallenge","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"UmaChallenger","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:8AxiamSDK13UmaChallengerV"},{"text":"?) -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AxiamGuardHandler","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:8AxiamSDK0A12GuardHandlera"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AxiamGuards\/requireAccess(_:resource:scope:umaChallenge:)","kind":"symbol"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/UmaChallenger":{"title":"UmaChallenger","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"UmaChallenger"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"UmaChallenger"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/UmaChallenger","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/umachallenger","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A configured "},{"code":"WWW-Authenticate: UMA","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" challenge emitter (CONTRACT.md §20.3, emit half)."}]},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/UmaChallenger/asURI":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"asURI"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/UmaChallenger\/asURI","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/umachallenger\/asuri","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The authorization server the caller should redeem the ticket at — normally this"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"deployment’s issuer, read from "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AxiamClient\/umaDiscover()","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" rather than concatenated by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"hand, for the same reason §12.3 rule 6 gives."}],"title":"asURI","role":"symbol"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/AxiamClient/umaDiscover()":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"umaDiscover"},{"kind":"text","text":"() "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"async"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":" -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Um